WEBVTT

00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:03.390
<b>Tawara Noodles</b>

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:30.250
<b>Chips</b>

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:30.250
<b>Edamame</b>

00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:29.570
Oh, you're awake.

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:54.720
<b>Poco's Udon World</b>

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:18.330
Souta! Souta!

00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:20.070
Episode 4: "Yashima"

00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:20.240
Huh? Sis?

00:02:23.150 --> 00:02:25.030
What's with the kid?

00:02:26.470 --> 00:02:31.250
Well, I'm bettin' it's Shinobu-chan's 
with some random woman.

00:02:31.490 --> 00:02:33.900
There it is. Her Nakajima bullying...

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:35.150
Heck no!

00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:37.940
Rinko, what kinda guy do ya think I am?!

00:02:38.450 --> 00:02:40.060
Then whose kid is it?

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:44.390
Souta!

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:47.480
Hey, he's terrified of you.

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:49.080
More than he was of me.

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:51.020
Huh? I wasn't tryin' to...

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:53.980
God, I'm just awful with kids!

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:56.010
If I so much as hold 'em, they start wailin'.

00:02:56.010 --> 00:02:57.380
Do I look that scary?

00:02:57.380 --> 00:02:57.740
Yep.

00:02:57.740 --> 00:02:59.240
Shinobu-chan, you shut your mouth!

00:03:00.050 --> 00:03:02.660
You'll get yours! Stupid! Stupid!

00:03:05.630 --> 00:03:07.930
Shinobu-chan hasn't changed one bit.

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:11.900
He'd always go home like that 
when he was a kid, too.

00:03:16.580 --> 00:03:19.170
I'm Souta's big sister.

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:20.740
My name's Rinko.

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:22.840
Can you tell me your name?

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:27.600
Poco.

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:30.650
Huh? That's your real name? 
One of those unconventional names?

00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:33.220
I figured that's what you'd comment on...

00:03:33.670 --> 00:03:37.570
Anyway, I'm taking care of him 
for a friend for a little while.

00:03:37.870 --> 00:03:39.230
Who's the friend?

00:03:39.230 --> 00:03:42.870
A friend from Tokyo. You wouldn't know them.

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:45.670
Oh, really? How long is "a little while"?

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:48.320
Until the end of my summer vacation?

00:03:50.650 --> 00:03:52.750
Is he<i> really </i>a friend's kid?

00:03:54.850 --> 00:03:57.750
Whoa! He forced himself in to hide!

00:03:59.770 --> 00:04:01.760
Let me go get him dressed.

00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:06.910
<i>Until the end of my summer vacation...</i>

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:08.810
These, too.

00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:11.270
<i>When I go back to Tokyo,</i>

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:13.750
<i>what will happen to Poco?</i>

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:17.050
<i>What will he eat?</i>

00:04:17.050 --> 00:04:18.140
<i>And... what will he eat?</i>

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:19.400
Souta?

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:22.160
Whoa!

00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:25.840
Poco, do you remember our promise?

00:04:26.450 --> 00:04:28.580
Pwomise?

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:31.140
But from now on,

00:04:31.140 --> 00:04:34.190
don't show your ears and tail 
in front of anyone but me, okay?

00:04:35.010 --> 00:04:37.750
Uh-huh. Pwomise!

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:40.500
Right. Promise.

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:48.060
It's clean...

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:51.050
You know, I <i>am</i> a housewife.

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:55.030
Actually, I came by today because I thought 
it was high time we tidied up the house.

00:04:55.330 --> 00:04:56.300
Oh, right...

00:04:58.050 --> 00:05:01.780
But you know... It's sad...

00:05:02.450 --> 00:05:04.960
Losin' the house we grew up in...

00:05:13.050 --> 00:05:14.040
Yeah.

00:05:19.780 --> 00:05:22.770
Hey, for lunch, let's go to Yashima.

00:05:22.770 --> 00:05:23.670
Sound good?

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:35.390
I haven't gone up to the top 
of Yashima in forever.

00:05:35.390 --> 00:05:39.170
I don't usually go all the way 
to Yashimaji Temple...

00:05:39.170 --> 00:05:40.840
Same here.

00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:43.210
It's been too long...

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:43.570
<b>have many children</b>

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:44.820
<b>Castle Remains</b>

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:44.820
<b>Throwing</b>

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:46.070
<b>We have a special path. Walk with us!</b>

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:46.070
<b>Driveway</b>

00:05:47.270 --> 00:05:48.730
Has Yashima...

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:50.200
<b>Welcome to Yashima</b>

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:50.200
<b>Lion Rock</b>

00:05:49.150 --> 00:05:52.470
always been this filled with tanuki?

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:52.950
<b>Ba-dum 
Ba-dum 
Ba-dum</b>

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:55.660
The tanuki are so cute, aren't they?

00:05:53.650 --> 00:05:54.720
<i>Wait...</i>

00:05:55.240 --> 00:05:56.960
<i>Could it be there's...</i>

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:56.960
Cute!

00:05:56.960 --> 00:05:59.750
<i>some connection between Yashima and Poco?</i>

00:06:00.180 --> 00:06:02.460
Here, put this on and...

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:05.460
You look just like a tanuki!

00:06:07.230 --> 00:06:09.720
No, it looks better on me!

00:06:11.240 --> 00:06:14.020
He's tryin' to be funny.

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:16.220
Be a dear and laugh for him, Poco-chan.

00:06:16.220 --> 00:06:18.410
<i>I wish I could just tell her!</i>

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:21.230
<b>Seto Inland Sea 
National Park
Yashima</b>

00:06:21.230 --> 00:06:23.230
<b>Shikoku Sacred Site #84</b>

00:06:23.230 --> 00:06:27.240
<b>Shikoku Sacred Site #84</b>

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:33.590
Look at that!

00:06:33.590 --> 00:06:34.370
Huh?

00:06:36.370 --> 00:06:38.870
Whoa! They're so big!

00:06:39.170 --> 00:06:39.870
They're tanuki?

00:06:40.180 --> 00:06:43.560
Wow! The shapeshifting 
tanuki of Yashima, huh...

00:06:44.180 --> 00:06:46.650
Hey, it says he's a god of family happiness.

00:06:46.650 --> 00:06:47.880
Better say a prayer!

00:06:48.190 --> 00:06:49.470
I'm goin' up ahead!

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:50.880
Hey, wait!

00:06:57.390 --> 00:07:00.890
<b>The Yashima Tasaburou Tanuki</b>

00:06:57.390 --> 00:07:00.890
<b>general head of
tanuki in Shikoku</b>

00:06:57.390 --> 00:07:00.890
<b>metamorphosis 
stood unchallenged
throughout Japan</b>

00:07:01.850 --> 00:07:05.730
There are stories of a shapeshifting 
tanuki appearing in these parts.

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:10.700
They say that the tanuki 
takes on a human appearance,

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:13.990
and lives in the form of a 
child for years and years.

00:07:15.720 --> 00:07:16.700
Poco...

00:07:17.180 --> 00:07:19.740
Could you be...

00:07:20.550 --> 00:07:22.890
a relative of this general or something?!

00:07:22.890 --> 00:07:24.670
Maybe you're super famous 
in the tanuki world?!

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:26.210
A VIP?! Are you a VIP?!

00:07:28.760 --> 00:07:32.010
<i>Every time he smiles, I get the 
sense that I'm being fooled!</i>

00:07:44.550 --> 00:07:46.770
They're pilgrims.

00:07:47.070 --> 00:07:50.440
They're on a long trip to visit lots of temples.

00:07:51.290 --> 00:07:53.290
Pilgwim.

00:07:53.710 --> 00:07:54.580
That's right.

00:07:54.820 --> 00:07:57.250
Poco-chan has to pray, too.

00:07:57.250 --> 00:07:59.450
Souta, give us some money to offer.

00:08:00.720 --> 00:08:02.690
Don't tell me you came empty-handed!

00:08:02.690 --> 00:08:04.190
You didn't even bring a wallet?!

00:08:04.190 --> 00:08:05.890
I'll pay ya back later!

00:08:14.730 --> 00:08:17.260
And he's so little. What a good boy.

00:08:17.610 --> 00:08:19.150
He really is!

00:08:20.650 --> 00:08:22.310
They praised you, huh?

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:23.600
He's bein' bashful.

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:31.690
<b>Fortunes</b>

00:08:31.690 --> 00:08:33.450
<b>Your Fortune: Bad Luck</b>

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:42.960
<b>Great Luck</b>

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:42.960
<b>Bad Luck</b>

00:08:35.510 --> 00:08:39.300
Yep. I had a feeling that's what you'd get.

00:08:39.300 --> 00:08:40.220
What does that mean?!

00:08:40.220 --> 00:08:41.960
What did you get, Poco-chan?

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:45.390
Oh! You got "good luck"—kichi!

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:46.710
<b>Your fortune: Good Luck</b>

00:08:45.690 --> 00:08:46.710
Chi?

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:49.020
Pon! Kan! Call with abandon!

00:08:49.020 --> 00:08:50.780
I knew you'd do that.

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:52.970
<b>My big sister</b>

00:08:50.780 --> 00:08:51.830
Chi?

00:08:51.260 --> 00:08:52.970
<b>is fond of 
mahjong.</b>

00:08:52.970 --> 00:08:59.720
<b>Fortune Slips/
Wish Plaques</b>

00:08:53.460 --> 00:08:57.080
We're supposed to tie 'em 
as high up as we can, right?

00:08:57.760 --> 00:08:59.720
Okay, I'm counting on you, Poco.

00:08:59.720 --> 00:09:01.970
Help me fix my bad luck!

00:09:06.340 --> 00:09:07.820
Ow, ow, ow...

00:09:07.820 --> 00:09:09.670
What's wrong? You okay?

00:09:09.670 --> 00:09:10.860
Yeah, I'm good...

00:09:13.860 --> 00:09:20.620
<b>Siblings 
in Their 
Thirties</b>

00:09:14.080 --> 00:09:15.800
Just my leg acting up...

00:09:16.260 --> 00:09:17.480
I'm getting old.

00:09:17.480 --> 00:09:20.620
I sympathize, but stop callin' yourself "old"!

00:09:23.890 --> 00:09:25.740
Let's sit over there.

00:09:25.740 --> 00:09:27.770
Poco-chan, how 'bout I buy you ice cream?

00:09:27.770 --> 00:09:28.590
Ice cweam?

00:09:28.590 --> 00:09:31.930
Uh... I thought you didn't bring your wallet.

00:09:32.250 --> 00:09:33.760
<b>Yashima Little Tanuki</b>

00:09:59.880 --> 00:10:01.290
Yummy!

00:10:01.520 --> 00:10:04.490
Hey, I just remembered...

00:10:04.490 --> 00:10:08.040
Didn't you, me, and Dad 
come to Yashima before?

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:10.920
Really? When was that?

00:10:11.230 --> 00:10:14.790
You know, probably when 
Mom was in the hospital.

00:10:14.790 --> 00:10:16.620
So on the way home from visiting her.

00:10:16.620 --> 00:10:18.930
Hmm... Did we really?

00:10:19.270 --> 00:10:22.240
We ate ice cream here then, too...

00:10:23.090 --> 00:10:26.270
Yummy, yummy!

00:10:26.790 --> 00:10:29.600
Uh... Hey, shouldn't you feed that to him?

00:10:29.910 --> 00:10:32.390
I know, but he's trying so hard.

00:10:32.390 --> 00:10:33.860
Give him a bit longer.

00:10:38.620 --> 00:10:40.850
B-But...

00:10:41.370 --> 00:10:42.770
He's makin' a mess!

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:51.150
Ah! I'm sorry. I didn't mean that.

00:10:51.450 --> 00:10:54.010
Ah... Er...

00:10:55.770 --> 00:10:57.640
It's okay, it's okay.

00:10:57.640 --> 00:10:58.930
We can just wipe it off.

00:10:59.350 --> 00:11:00.130
Okay?

00:11:00.370 --> 00:11:04.420
Wh-What do I do now, Souta? 
He looks super sad...

00:11:04.420 --> 00:11:07.160
Well, yeah, you can be kind of harsh.

00:11:07.160 --> 00:11:10.390
I know that better than anyone!

00:11:13.980 --> 00:11:16.480
<b>Tile Throwing</b>

00:11:13.980 --> 00:11:16.480
<b>Lion Rock Tea House</b>

00:11:13.980 --> 00:11:16.480
<b>Seto Inland Sea National Park, Yashima</b>

00:11:19.620 --> 00:11:22.340
Why am I so bad with little kids?

00:11:21.420 --> 00:11:22.130
Here.

00:11:22.760 --> 00:11:26.750
You, on the other hand... Kids and 
animals have always liked you.

00:11:27.210 --> 00:11:29.680
I can't deny that...

00:11:27.610 --> 00:11:28.490
Bye-bye.

00:11:30.200 --> 00:11:33.860
Still... I think I regret it.

00:11:34.360 --> 00:11:37.430
Not givin' Dad any grandkids.

00:11:39.050 --> 00:11:41.010
It was my decision, but...

00:11:41.510 --> 00:11:44.640
If I had a kid, would it 
have changed anything?

00:11:45.400 --> 00:11:49.740
Did I choose the wrong path?
I have to wonder sometimes...

00:11:50.730 --> 00:11:53.170
I just don't know.

00:11:56.150 --> 00:11:57.220
Me, neither.

00:11:57.610 --> 00:11:58.750
Really?

00:11:59.050 --> 00:12:01.190
In the end, I never got Dad

00:12:01.190 --> 00:12:03.320
to appreciate my Web design work.

00:12:04.080 --> 00:12:07.050
I wonder if going to Tokyo 
was the right decision.

00:12:09.450 --> 00:12:11.220
Oh, jeez.

00:12:11.220 --> 00:12:14.640
Whenever we're together,
we end up reminiscing.

00:12:15.200 --> 00:12:16.340
What's wrong with that?

00:12:16.840 --> 00:12:19.210
We never used to talk like this.

00:12:23.890 --> 00:12:24.920
I remember now!

00:12:24.920 --> 00:12:25.520
Huh?

00:12:25.940 --> 00:12:28.760
I remember coming to 
Yashima with you and Dad.

00:12:30.080 --> 00:12:31.010
Souta.

00:12:31.330 --> 00:12:33.480
If ya hold the tile vertical,

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:35.050
it'll fly real far.

00:12:37.280 --> 00:12:38.110
Poco.

00:12:39.300 --> 00:12:41.360
I'll teach you how to throw those.

00:12:41.860 --> 00:12:44.320
How to throw?

00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:49.080
Hold the tile vertical...

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:50.030
Vertical...

00:12:50.330 --> 00:12:51.120
Right.

00:12:51.790 --> 00:12:52.680
Here we go!

00:12:53.140 --> 00:12:54.100
One,

00:12:53.570 --> 00:12:54.550
One,

00:12:54.550 --> 00:12:55.520
two...

00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:56.000
two...

00:12:56.330 --> 00:12:57.080
Three!

00:12:57.080 --> 00:12:57.770
Three!

00:13:10.480 --> 00:13:14.360
Think that cancels out my bad luck?

00:13:14.610 --> 00:13:17.610
No, I think this and that 
are two different matters.

00:13:17.610 --> 00:13:18.620
Cancel!

00:13:29.030 --> 00:13:31.040
<b>Work</b>

00:13:29.030 --> 00:13:31.040
<b>Incoming Call</b>

00:13:34.250 --> 00:13:35.790
You don't need to answer that?

00:13:36.490 --> 00:13:37.870
I'll call them back later.

00:13:38.450 --> 00:13:39.880
How long do you have off?

00:13:40.300 --> 00:13:43.050
It's sort of up for discussion.

00:13:43.500 --> 00:13:45.910
Are ya sure you can take so much time off?

00:13:46.230 --> 00:13:49.160
Also, are Poco-chan's parents okay with this?

00:13:49.160 --> 00:13:51.310
Yeah, it's fine.

00:13:51.750 --> 00:13:54.320
Well, one way or another, 
your sister's worried.

00:14:01.770 --> 00:14:03.820
<b>Shikoku Village</b>

00:14:13.650 --> 00:14:15.590
Souta, leaf!

00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:18.670
He's cheered right back up.

00:14:19.120 --> 00:14:20.610
Thank goodness.

00:14:20.910 --> 00:14:23.970
I don't deal with kids much.

00:14:24.440 --> 00:14:28.430
I just don't know how to act with them.

00:14:29.600 --> 00:14:30.400
But...

00:14:31.640 --> 00:14:33.440
When I look at Poco-chan, I...

00:14:34.220 --> 00:14:35.310
You what?

00:14:35.310 --> 00:14:37.450
I wonder what this feeling is...

00:14:38.350 --> 00:14:39.310
Who knows?

00:14:40.520 --> 00:14:43.610
Why did you decide to take charge of Poco?

00:14:43.910 --> 00:14:45.320
Weren't you concerned?

00:14:45.320 --> 00:14:49.300
Well, you could say I'm 
always concerned, in a way...

00:14:49.300 --> 00:14:50.660
Really?

00:14:52.030 --> 00:14:53.900
Huh? Where's Poco-chan?

00:14:53.900 --> 00:14:54.510
Huh?

00:14:55.240 --> 00:14:56.140
Poco?

00:14:59.450 --> 00:15:00.720
Do you think he...

00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:02.540
<b>Vine Bridge 
Entrance</b>

00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:02.540
<b>Notice:
No more than 20 people 
on the bridge at one time.
Please cross quietly. Those 
who cannot cross, please 
use the alternate entrance.</b>

00:15:05.670 --> 00:15:08.220
Souta! Souta!

00:15:08.480 --> 00:15:09.830
Souta!

00:15:11.760 --> 00:15:12.890
That's dangerous!

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:15.460
Souta! Souta!

00:15:13.240 --> 00:15:15.460
Poco-chan, that's dangerous!

00:15:15.460 --> 00:15:17.220
Souta! Souta!

00:15:15.460 --> 00:15:17.220
Don't bounce on it!

00:15:20.440 --> 00:15:22.280
Souta!

00:15:22.580 --> 00:15:25.520
Owie!

00:15:24.090 --> 00:15:25.520
What did I tell you?

00:15:26.290 --> 00:15:28.120
D-Don't move...

00:15:29.290 --> 00:15:31.260
I'm... I'm on my way...

00:15:33.220 --> 00:15:36.150
What are ya doin'? Hurry up!

00:15:38.190 --> 00:15:40.610
You know I have an extreme fear

00:15:40.610 --> 00:15:43.420
of high places and bridges like this!

00:15:43.420 --> 00:15:44.420
My hands sweat like crazy!

00:15:44.910 --> 00:15:47.460
Oh, good grief! This is no time for that!

00:15:47.910 --> 00:15:49.060
How pathetic!

00:15:49.060 --> 00:15:50.060
S-S—

00:15:50.720 --> 00:15:54.710
S-Stop! Don't shake the bridge!

00:15:57.750 --> 00:16:00.180
Poco-chan, I'll be right there.

00:16:00.990 --> 00:16:03.150
Just wait right there a bit, okay?

00:16:07.900 --> 00:16:08.690
Rin...

00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:19.120
Poco-chan...

00:16:22.810 --> 00:16:24.760
It's okay, it's okay.

00:16:26.990 --> 00:16:32.520
"The Iya Valley vine bridge

00:16:32.520 --> 00:16:38.240
sways back and forth,

00:16:38.540 --> 00:16:43.900
but if you hold hands,

00:16:43.900 --> 00:16:50.860
there's nothing to fear,"

00:16:51.730 --> 00:16:52.530
they say.

00:16:54.340 --> 00:16:57.870
See? It's not scary.

00:17:02.350 --> 00:17:05.070
Good. Let's cross this bridge, okay?

00:17:05.980 --> 00:17:06.560
Wait!

00:17:07.350 --> 00:17:10.880
<i>I'm</i> scared! Poco!

00:17:16.710 --> 00:17:18.460
There, we made it.

00:17:18.760 --> 00:17:19.900
Made it!

00:17:24.570 --> 00:17:28.090
Made it, made it, made it...

00:17:26.400 --> 00:17:26.980
<i>His hands...</i>

00:17:28.090 --> 00:17:30.260
<i>are so small.</i>

00:17:33.430 --> 00:17:36.530
Poco-chan, are you lonely 
with just you and Souta?

00:17:39.440 --> 00:17:40.990
Do you love Souta?

00:17:41.260 --> 00:17:43.030
I love Souta!

00:17:45.250 --> 00:17:47.990
Which do you love more, food or Souta?

00:17:49.010 --> 00:17:50.040
S-Souta!

00:17:50.340 --> 00:17:52.760
Oh? Really?

00:17:53.270 --> 00:17:55.130
You had to think about it, didn't you?

00:17:58.880 --> 00:17:59.820
Rin, too.

00:18:00.440 --> 00:18:01.760
I love Rin, too!

00:18:07.010 --> 00:18:09.450
Th-Thank you...

00:18:11.230 --> 00:18:13.030
I'm glad.

00:18:13.560 --> 00:18:15.780
Yep, I'm glad!

00:18:23.170 --> 00:18:24.450
I thought I was gonna die...

00:18:24.730 --> 00:18:26.220
Souta!

00:18:27.900 --> 00:18:31.140
What's come over me? My heart's all tight...

00:18:31.460 --> 00:18:33.210
I-Is this maternal instinct?!

00:18:33.710 --> 00:18:36.080
Uh... Probably?

00:18:46.320 --> 00:18:47.120
Up we go!

00:18:50.430 --> 00:18:54.360
Oh, yeah. Poco-chan, 
do you love Shinobu-chan?

00:18:54.660 --> 00:18:56.380
She means Nakajima.

00:18:57.200 --> 00:18:59.570
Na... Nakaji...

00:19:04.400 --> 00:19:06.380
Looks like he's torn!

00:19:07.770 --> 00:19:09.370
Nakajima...

00:19:09.370 --> 00:19:10.870
<b>Staff Station</b>

00:20:31.290 --> 00:20:37.000
<b>Gaogao-chan and</b>

00:20:33.870 --> 00:20:37.000
<b>The Blue Sky</b>

00:20:37.650 --> 00:20:39.300
<i>The Tale of Gaogao-chan</i>

00:20:37.800 --> 00:20:43.010
<b>Episode 4: 
"Gaogao-chan and the Taste of First Love"</b>

00:20:39.300 --> 00:20:42.270
<i>and the Taste of First Love!</i>

00:20:43.580 --> 00:20:45.610
<i>Thanks to Gaogao-chan,</i>

00:20:45.610 --> 00:20:47.910
<i>it's another peaceful day on Earth.</i>

00:20:48.280 --> 00:20:49.770
<i>And on this peaceful day...</i>

00:20:50.540 --> 00:20:53.850
<i>Let's play the "Guess What I Like" game!</i>

00:20:53.850 --> 00:20:55.780
<i>Yay! Yay!</i>

00:20:55.780 --> 00:20:58.020
<i>Okay, I'll start.</i>

00:20:58.020 --> 00:21:00.050
<i>I like something</i>

00:21:00.050 --> 00:21:01.900
<i>that's steamy hot and white,</i>

00:21:01.900 --> 00:21:04.370
<i>and fills you with happiness just seeing it.</i>

00:21:04.370 --> 00:21:05.700
<i>Rice balls!</i>

00:21:05.700 --> 00:21:06.280
<i>That's right!</i>

00:21:06.680 --> 00:21:08.620
<i>You're next, Flower-san!</i>

00:21:08.920 --> 00:21:11.360
<i>Me? I don't have anything....</i>

00:21:11.360 --> 00:21:12.850
<i>Liar!</i>

00:21:12.850 --> 00:21:16.090
<i>Okay, he's really thorny,</i>

00:21:16.090 --> 00:21:17.860
<i>but deep down, he's a romantic,</i>

00:21:17.860 --> 00:21:21.410
<i>and he's really cool and chic, 
like he was brought up on the backstreets...</i>

00:21:21.410 --> 00:21:23.130
<i>Gaogao-chan!</i>

00:21:24.050 --> 00:21:26.570
<i>Don't worry. Just leave this to us!</i>

00:21:26.570 --> 00:21:28.820
<i>A friend in need is a friend, indeed!</i>

00:21:28.820 --> 00:21:29.260
<i>Huh?</i>

00:21:29.940 --> 00:21:31.580
<i>Gaogao-chan!</i>

00:21:31.580 --> 00:21:35.960
<i>Flower-san says she thinks you're cool!</i>

00:21:36.260 --> 00:21:37.010
<i>Gao?</i>

00:21:37.010 --> 00:21:38.840
<i>Jeez, Mimi-chan!</i>

00:21:39.270 --> 00:21:41.830
<i>And so, Gaogao-chan and</i>

00:21:41.830 --> 00:21:45.650
<i>Timid Flower-san agreed to go on a date.</i>

00:21:47.380 --> 00:21:51.060
<i>Listen up! You'd better make this 
a great date, or I'll be mad!</i>

00:21:51.060 --> 00:21:52.290
<i>I mean it!</i>

00:21:52.290 --> 00:21:54.460
<b>Date
Route</b>

00:21:52.290 --> 00:21:54.460
<b>Treasure</b>

00:21:52.290 --> 00:21:54.460
<b>Beast</b>

00:21:52.290 --> 00:21:54.460
<b>Death</b>

00:21:52.700 --> 00:21:54.720
<i>We planned out the perfect route for your date!</i>

00:21:55.120 --> 00:21:57.680
<i>Momo-chan, maybe we shouldn't.</i>

00:21:55.120 --> 00:22:00.840
<b>Top Secret</b>

00:21:57.680 --> 00:21:59.640
<i>A flower, in love with a lion...</i>

00:21:59.640 --> 00:22:00.840
<i>It's not right.</i>

00:22:01.340 --> 00:22:04.340
<i>Don't worry. This date'll 
go off without a hitch!</i>

00:22:06.620 --> 00:22:10.720
<i>Gaogao-chan, I want to cross that bridge.</i>

00:22:09.220 --> 00:22:10.720
<b>Swaying Bridge</b>

00:22:16.040 --> 00:22:18.500
<i>Gaogao-chan, I love you!</i>

00:22:19.730 --> 00:22:23.230
<i>Why does my chest feel tight?</i>

00:22:23.560 --> 00:22:24.740
<i>It's the suspension bridge effect.</i>

00:22:25.010 --> 00:22:26.990
<i>Uh-huh, it's the suspension bridge effect.</i>

00:22:30.210 --> 00:22:31.530
<i>Is this feeling...</i>

00:22:32.660 --> 00:22:33.680
<i>Maternal instinct?</i>

